##### Who I am

Hi! I’m Evan. I was born and raised in the Greater Cincinnati Area where I spent much of my childhood, 
outside, learning about the [fossils](https://www.cincymuseum.org/2022/10/07/the-cincinnati-arch/), [geology](https://ohiodnr.gov/wps/wcm/connect/gov/e1c431e3-3ff4-4eb1-812f-7d0802127b81/Glacial+Map+of+Ohio.pdf?MOD=AJPERES&CVID=ne.WIDF), [plants](https://ohiodnr.gov/discover-and-learn/plants-trees/broad-leaf-trees/pawpaw-asimina-triloba), and [animals](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opheodrys_aestivus) of the Ohio River Valley. I blame and 
thank my childhood for instilling in me an indelible interest in exploring the beauty and 
mysteries of the natural world.

I got my bachelor's in biology from [Miami University](https://miamioh.edu), where I also dabbled in neuroscience, 
computer science, and bioinformatics, but environmental science has always had my heart. 
Shortly before graduating with my bachelor’s, I applied and was accepted into a PhD program 
for environmental biology (wherein I would’ve focused on bioremediation research in 
eastern deciduous forests). 

But, [my husband](https://linkedin.com/in/emil-sayahi/) got a job that was pulling us out to San Francisco and I decided to decline the offer. 
We moved out here in May 2025, just weeks after I graduated. I was unemployed from then until about 
the start of 2026, when I started a tech-adjacent marketing job. My goal is to, somehow, get back 
into environmental science proper, whether through a job or grad school, in the next year or two or three. 

That was a relevant introduction if you’re interested in reading the "Science" part of this blog. 
But there is more to me than that!

I also like to think and write about a wide variety of other things. There’s nothing I love more 
than to go down random rabbit holes, and I have a wide range of hobbies, from [mudlarking](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mudlark) to 
[maritime history](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinking_of_the_SS_Arctic) to [poetry](https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poems/48417/high-windows). Until now, almost all of my writing has been on notebook paper, 
and has included everything from short stories to essays to thoughts on random goings-on in 
my day-to-day life. My goal is to publish that stuff here from now on, and that will be what 
you’ll find under the "Random Thoughts" part of this blog.

##### What you will find under "Science"

- My thoughts on EnvSci articles, research, topics, & issues
- My ideas for future EnvSci research & experiments
- Blog posts about my progress on EnvSci-related coding projects (if I ever get around to it!)
- (Potentially) Non-EnvSci science stuff that interests me

##### What you will find under "Random Thoughts"

- Random thoughts, ideas, musings, etc.
- Essays & blog posts unrelated to science
- Maybe even some art, eventually (e.g. poetry, drawings, comics)

##### Why this website exists

- To participate in & contribute to the EnvSci--and broader scientific--community while I’m still employed in a different field
- To explore areas of research to potentially pursue in grad school
- To share my thoughts, in a relatively coherent manner, with friends & family I don't get to talk to on a daily basis
- For my future self
- For anyone out there interested in the things I write about :)

Thanks for reading!
